Hi Greg, Sasha,

Thanks for queuing the 6.12.y series and the two fixes from October
19th, and for 6.18.58.

Here is the rest of what has been merged in mod-orphan for AX.25,
NET/ROM and ROSE, for 6.12.y and 6.18.y.
None of these 26 patches has been sent to stable before.
Most are memory-safety and locking fixes, a few are protocol fixes
that stop links from hanging.

NET/ROM:
1. netrom: linearize and validate lengths in nr_rx_frame() (Stanislav Fort)
2. netrom: require full NET/ROM headers in nr_route_frame() (Greg Kroah-Har=
tman)
3. net: netrom: validate source address in nr_find_socket() (Mashiro Chen)
4. netrom: bound fragment reassembly in nr_queue_rx_frame()
5. netrom: use a single lock for the node and neighbour lists
6. netrom: look up and update routes in one critical section
7. netrom: fix reference count leak in nr_rt_device_down (Junjie Cao)
8. netrom: clear nr_neigh->ax25 under the routing lock in nr_link_failed()
9. netrom: fix nr_node leak when nr_del_node() removes the last route

AX.25:
10. ax25: fix OOB read after address header strip in ax25_rcv() (Ashutosh D=
esai)
11. ax25: check frame length in ax25_decode() and ax25_rx_iframe()
12. net: ax25: fix integer overflow in ax25_rx_fragment() (Mashiro Chen)
13. ax25: serialise the transmission of I frames on a connection
14. ax25: don't create two connections for the same link in ax25_send_frame=
()
15. ax25: read the connection's ax25_dev only once when walking ax25_list
16. ax25: wait for ax25_send_frame() before detaching the connections
of a device
17. ax25: don't accept frames on a device that is going down
18. ax25: send a private copy of each I frame
19. ax25: send unacknowledged I frames again when a link is re-established
20. ax25: don't free an incoming SABM skb left on the listener's queue

ROSE:
21. rose: clear stale N(R)/N(S) before (re)transmitting a data frame
22. rose: clear through routes when a neighbour is removed from the tables
23. rose: restart the link of a neighbour created over a live AX.25 connect=
ion
24. rose: process received frames and send with the socket locked
25. rose: clear the circuits of a neighbour that restarts the link
26. rose: bring up the link of the preferred route passed over by a
connect request

The list above is grouped by protocol.
In the mboxes, the patches follow the mod-orphan merge order, which
must be kept, since several of them touch the same functions.

The two attached mboxes hold the 26 patches, one mbox per branch.
Each patch carries a "(cherry picked from commit <id>)" trailer with
the mod-orphan git id.

- 6.18.y: the mbox applies with "git am" on top of v6.18.58 plus the
two patches queued on October 19th.
- 6.12.y: the mbox applies with "git am" on top of v6.12.114 plus the
twelve patches now in queue-6.12.

The backports are the mod-orphan commits with one change: patch 20
used kmalloc_obj(), which these branches do not have, and now uses
kmalloc(sizeof(ax25_digi), GFP_ATOMIC) as the surrounding code does.
I left out one mod-orphan commit, "rose: fix sk_filter_trim_cap()
compatibility across kernel versions", which only concerns building
the out-of-tree modules against several kernel versions.

As on my earlier batches, the mod-orphan commits carrying my callsign
as author name use my real name here.
Seven patches had a "Co-Authored-By:" line for the AI assistant I
used; in the backports it is an "Assisted-by:" line, as
Documentation/process asks.

Testing:
- each patch builds on both branches (net/ax25, net/netrom and
net/rose, W=3D1, KASAN enabled), with no warnings and no errors;
- checkpatch reports nothing beyond style remarks in the original commits;
- all 26 fixes are part of the module set running on our production
AX.25 / NET/ROM / ROSE nodes; the complete set has been in service
since October 17th, and the older patches since September.

Thanks,
Bernard, F6BVP


